{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdLd7qRvP3HaNU28Ae8h3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-282 is complete and committed. Summary of what was delivered on `llm/train/p0-g3-WI-282-eb40` (commit `b396d2f`):\n\n## What the WI does\nEnforces the train-build `WI:` trailer at **commit time**, closing the gap that let a malformed trailer block silently cost a build+review cycle (train `p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9`, 2026-07-23: `reviewed_train_head` skipped the untrailered tip to an older CHANGES-REQUESTED head and parked an APPROVED train as rework).\n\n**Primary — commit-msg floor** (`project-trajectory/hooks/commit-msg`): a **pure-sh** check that runs before the Python message scan (so it holds even without Python). On `llm/train/*`, a build commit must carry a parseable `WI: WI-<n>` trailer, verified via `git interpret-trailers --parse` — git's *own* parser, so the floor accepts exactly what the integrator's `%(trailers)` read later resolves. It refuses with an actionable message naming the exact fix. Sanctioned `integrate:`/`telemetry:`/`review:`/`blocked:` subjects and a `Blocked-WI:` disposition stay legal.\n\n**Secondary — loud diagnostic** (`agent_dispatch.warn_reviewed_head_slip`): when the reviewed head isn't the newest substantive build commit, it journals `reviewed-head-trailer-slip` naming both SHAs — so a slip reads as a slip, not honest dissent. Runs before the verdict gate, so it's visible even on the exact park path from the live failure.\n\nOne shared source (`agent_common.SANCTIONED_TRAIN_SUBJECT_PREFIXES`) keeps the floor (sh) and the diagnostic (py) from disagreeing; the enforcement-audit records the Prose→Harness move.\n\n## Verification (all on the pinned 3.11.9 venv)\n- **Full suite green: 1419 passed, 5 skipped** (the WI-done bar) on the final tree.\n- Commit-msg floor tested 13 ways (malformed refused with the exact fix; all sanctioned shapes + `Blocked-WI` pass; off-train vacuous; holds without Python); diagnostic tested both directions.\n- ruff format + lint clean; pre-commit floor passed at commit; **my own commit passed my own floor** — its trailers parse as `WI=WI-282, Train=…, Base=…`.\n\n## Design note\nI first shipped this as a standalone `check_wi_trailer.py`, but the spec's *\"no spine SR — meta harness layer\"* / *\"intra-module\"* design and the component-containment gate (a new module is \"uncontained\") pointed to the hook-resident pure-sh implementation instead — reworked to that, with no new module or spine row. The arch-map + dashboard were regenerated for the new function (integrator re-regenerates on the composed tree). I left `status.md`/`log.md`/`work-items.csv` cells untouched — the `done` flip + spec archival is the integrator's close-ritual."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":309938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f51d775d-365f-4a06-87af-1743fc0e0a5e","uuid":"4a215a3a-e336-4927-8bf0-9ed746cc2449","request_id":"req_011CdLd7oByxi2WRvS6zrBkV"}
